68% year-over-year.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said data-center revenue was $194 billion for FY2026, up 68% year over year.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "party_statement", "event_time": "FY2026", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e3", "quote": "We look ahead, we expect sequential revenue growth throughout calendar 2026, exceeding what was included in the $500 billion Blackwell and Rubin revenue opportunity we shared last year.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA expected sequential revenue growth throughout calendar 2026 and said the outlook exceeded the previously shared $500 billion Blackwell and Rubin revenue opportunity.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "party_statement", "event_time": "Calendar 2026 outlook", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e4", "quote": "We expect most of our growth to be driven by data center.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said the Q1 FY2027 revenue growth was expected to be driven mostly by data center.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "party_statement", "event_time": "Q1 FY2027 outlook", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e5", "quote": "For the full year, we continue to see gross margins in the mid-70s.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA continued to expect full-year gross margins in the mid-70s.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "party_statement", "event_time": "FY2027 outlook", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e6", "quote": "For the full year, we expect non-GAAP operating expenses to grow in the low 40s on a year-over-year basis as we continue to invest in our expanding opportunity set.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said FY2027 non-GAAP operating expenses were expected to grow in the low 40s year over year.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "party_statement", "event_time": "FY2027 outlook", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e7", "quote": "For the full year fiscal year '27, we expect GAAP and non-GAAP tax rates to be in between 7% and 19%, excluding any discrete items and material changes to our tax environment.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said FY2027 GAAP and non-GAAP tax rates were expected to be 7%–19%, excluding discrete items and material tax-environment changes.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "party_statement", "event_time": "FY2027 outlook", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e8", "quote": "We shipped our first Vera Rubin samples to customers earlier this week, and we remain on track to commence production shipments in the second half of the year.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA had shipped its first Vera Rubin samples and remained on track to begin production shipments in the second half of 2026.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "party_statement", "event_time": "Second half of 2026", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e9", "quote": "Analyst expectations for 2026 CapEx across the top 5 cloud providers and hyperscalers who collectively account for a little over 50% of our data center revenue are up nearly $120 billion since the start of the year and approaching $700 billion.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said analyst expectations for 2026 capital expenditure by the top five cloud providers and hyperscalers were approaching $700 billion, nearly $120 billion above the start-of-year expectations.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "Analyst expectations, as reported by Colette Kress", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "third_party_view", "event_time": "Calendar 2026", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e10", "quote": "While small amounts of H200 products for China-based customers were approved by the U.S. government, we have yet to generate any revenue. And we do not know whether any imports will be allowed into China.", "one_line": "NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said the U.S. government had approved small amounts of H200 products for China-based customers, NVIDIA had no resulting revenue, and whether imports into China would be allowed remained unknown.", "speaker": "Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "party_statement", "event_time": "As of 2026-02-25", "created_seq": 1, "created_from_input": "truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25"}, {"evidence_id": "e11", "quote": "Fiscal year revenue was a record $215.9 billion, up 65% from a year ago.", "one_line": "NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year.", "speaker": "NVIDIA Corporation", "original_who": "", "original_day": "2026-02-25", "tier": "fact", "event_time": "FY2026", "created_seq": 3, "created_from_input": "edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000019:q4fy26cfocommentary.htm"}, {"evidence_id": "e12", "quote": "Data Center revenue for the fourth quarter was a record $62.3 billion, up 75% from a year ago and up 22% sequentially, driven by the major platform shifts – accelerated computing and AI.", "one_line": "NVIDIA reported Q4 FY2026 Data Center revenue of $62.3 billion, up 75% year over year and 22% sequentially.", "speaker": "NVIDIA Corporation", "