{"call_id": 9, "purpose": "judge", "answer_json": "{\"changed\": true, \"cites\": [\"e50\", \"e51\"], \"cites_views\": [], \"pushes\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"e50\", \"push\": \"none\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e51\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}], \"reasons\": \"Rung 1 is the better-supported judgment, but the outcome is not established: the target date is still in the future, and e51 is a party statement that the factory is planned to come online in 2027, not confirmation that it is online. e50 establishes that letters of intent were signed for a partnership, but does not establish the factory's completion or operating status.\", \"rung\": 1, \"why_changed\": \"This is the first judgment, so changed is true.\"}", "input_tokens": 894, "output_tokens": 427, "cost_usd": 0.000303, "seconds": 5.3}
{"call_id": 10, "purpose": "judge", "answer_json": "{\"changed\": true, \"cites\": [\"e52\"], \"cites_views\": [], \"pushes\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"e52\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}], \"reasons\": \"Rung 1 is the better-supported judgment: NVIDIA states that NAVER and NVIDIA plan to expand the GAK Sejong buildout from 55 megawatts to 200 megawatts by 2028. This is a forward-looking party statement, not confirmation that the deployment has reached 200 megawatts; the outcome is therefore not established as fact.\", \"rung\": 1, \"why_changed\": \"This is the first judgment. The announced plan supports rung 1, while leaving execution by the deadline unconfirmed.\"}", "input_tokens": 774, "output_tokens": 576, "cost_usd": 0.000365, "seconds": 7.1}
{"call_id": 11, "purpose": "judge", "answer_json": "{\"changed\": false, \"cites\": [\"e3\", \"e19\", \"e24\", \"e34\", \"e42\", \"e44\", \"e53\"], \"cites_views\": [], \"pushes\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"e3\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e19\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e24\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e34\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e42\", \"push\": \"none\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e44\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e53\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}], \"reasons\": \"Rung 1 remains the better directional judgment, but commencement is not established: no fact confirms that Vera Rubin production shipments have begun. The strongest support is Kress’s May 20 statement that shipments were “on track” to commence “starting in Q3” 2026 (e34), which points toward commencement before the deadline. NVIDIA’s expectation of shipments in the second half of FY2027 (e24) is supportive but does not by itself establish commencement by December 31. The broader revenue outlook, planned first cloud deployments, and planned GAK Sejong infrastructure are indirect positive indications (e3, e19, e53). The platform announcement is not evidence that production shipments commenced (e42), and the company’s warning about production delays and supply-demand challenges weighs against the positive case (e44). Missing confirmation is not evidence that shipments did not occur.\", \"rung\": 1, \"why_changed\": \"The rung and its key supporting guidance remain unchanged. The additional planned GAK Sejong deployment (e53) is indirect and does not establish or materially alter the shipment outlook; no evidence changes the central Q3 2026 on-track statement or the stated production-delay risk.\"}", "input_tokens": 1624, "output_tokens": 1482, "cost_usd": 0.000903, "seconds": 22.9}
{"call_id": 12, "purpose": "judge", "answer_json": "{\"changed\": false, \"cites\": [\"e2\", \"e3\", \"e12\", \"e26\", \"e27\", \"e31\", \"e52\", \"e54\"], \"cites_views\": [], \"pushes\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"e2\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e3\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e12\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e26\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e27\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e31\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e52\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e54\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}], \"reasons\": \"Rung 3 (Neutral: at least $350 billion and less than $450 billion) remains the best-supported judgment, not an established FY2027 outcome. NVIDIA reported FY2026 data-center revenue of $194 billion and Q1 FY2027 revenue of $75 billion, up 21% sequentially (e2, e31; the Q4 FY2026 figure was $62.3 billion, e12). Reaching $450 billion for FY2027 would require another $375 billion across the remaining three quarters, or an average of $125 billion per quarter; reaching $350 billion requires an average of about $92 billion. The CFO expects sequential growth throughout calendar 2026 and says it will exceed the previously shared $500 billion Blackwell and Rubin revenue opportunity (e3), which supports further growth but does not establish that opportunity as FY2027 data-center revenue or quantify FY2027 quarterly results. The planned capacity expansion and $500-billion-plus partnership are directionally supportive, but are plans rather than reported FY2027 revenue (e52, e54). NVIDIA also identified data-center capacity, energy, and capital constraints and its effective foreclosure from China's data-center market as risks (e26, e27). On balance, the evidence favors substantial growth consistent with rung 3 over the more demanding $450 billion threshold, while leaving meaningful uncertainty.\", \"rung\": 3, \"why_changed\": \"The rung and the central revenue figures supporting it are unchanged from the previous conclusion. The additional partnership and infrastructure plans are supportive but do not quantify FY2027 revenue or change the key threshold analysis.\"}", "input_tokens": 1899, "output_tokens": 1939, "cost_usd": 0.001159, "seconds": 25.8}
